# R39 snag #2 focused fixture — block-final dedent case
# (match-arm-else body).
#
# Pre-fix: the trailing comment on the LAST stmt of a match-arm's
# `else:` body dedented out of the entire match block, sometimes to
# the enclosing function's scope or even to top-level. Same class as
# the struct-last-field case (block-final dedent); different context
# to guard against a per-block-context regression.
#
# Post-fix: `format_block_stmts` calls
# `emit_trailing_comment_after(stmt.span.end)` after each stmt in ANY
# block context (function bodies, if/elif/else, match-arm bodies,
# try/catch, with, select), so the trailing comment on the
# else-body's last stmt stays at the else-body's indentation (12
# spaces = case-body indent + else-body indent).
#
# Correctness signal: `# belongs to else` appears on the SAME line as
# `pass` at 12-space indent (match block = 4, arm else = 8, arm body
# stmt = 12).

void apply(int x):
    match x:
        case 1:
            print("one")
        else:
            pass  # belongs to else

int main():
    apply(1)
    apply(2)
    return 0
